      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BEATTY (1) is the one to beat after a dominant Belgravia Stakes win, scoring by 1.3L after rounding up his rivals from the back. A better draw this time should see him closer in the run and his best run of his debut campaign was over this track and trip. Giving his rivals weight but he might still be too good. ROGER (4) brings the fresh blood, being unbeaten and scoring an Open 3YO race impressively, with that form tying through Treasured Legacy who was placed in the Burgess Queen on Tuesday. Form stacks up and it wouldn't surprise to see him knock off BEATTY. GODSPEED (5) finished strongly from the back of the pack to finish 2L away in the Belgravia. Drawn sticky again here, but he shouldn't be too far off the lead and CJP sticks. Out in trip looks a big tick and he can play a leading role. SWIFT RULER (3) can bounce back dropping to 1400m. HE'S A MACHINO (2) looks better suited out to 1400m and can be thereabouts.",
